  ],
  "notes": "EIS sweeps (0.01 Hz-1 kHz) at 5-100% SOC and 0.12 A constant-current capacity tests on LFP cells. File names read IFR14500, a cylindrical 14500 size, while the registry calls the cell a pouch cell. All 11 capacity-test CSV headers were inspected: discharge mode D-CC at 0.12 A to 2.00 V, equivalent to 0.2C using the source nominal 0.6 Ah. Their time-series headers are Time(S),Cur(A),Vol(V), with no temperature. All 440 EIS CSV headers were checked: temperature is recorded only against frequency, always 20 C, with no time column. This is not evidence of a delivered cell-temperature time series; generic temperature logging and temperature time-series availability must be distinguished. The charge rate and upper cutoff remain unsupported."
 },
